    "code_current_through_note": "eCode360 shows no currency date for the Newtown Area Zoning Jointure code. The latest codified amendment seen is JMZO Ord. No. 2022-02 (adopted 7/21/2025).",
    "code_caution": "Four New Laws are not yet in the code text: Ord. No. 2026-01 (B-17 Elderly House Usage, Article VIII, adopted 2026-05-19), Ord. No. 2026-03 (Article VIII, 2026-08-19), Ord. No. 2022-03 and Ord. No. 2022-01 (2026-05-19). They were not read and may change Article VIII. The ordinance is shared with Upper Makefield and Wrightstown, so check which districts are mapped in Newtown Township.",
    "checks": [
      "A residential accessory structure (use H-3) may include 'No greater than one residential accessory apartment for domestic servants, caretakers employed on the premises, occasional gratuitous guests, or for permanent residence of family members related by blood, marriage, or adoption' (Article VIII, 803 H-3.4)",
      "Use H-3 is a use by right in JM, CM, CR-1, CR-2, R-1, R-2, VR-1, VR-4, OR, VC-1, VC-2 and QA. In TC-2 and CC it is allowed only as accessory to an existing residential use (in CC an existing nonconforming one). In RI and RI-A it is a conditional use. PC lists a 'Residential Accessory Building, use H-3' but permits no dwelling, so ask. PS, PS-2, TC, LI (H-3 repealed by JMZO Ord. 2014-01), O-LI, QA-A, MS, MSA, EIR and POS do not list it (400 to 409, 500 to 502, 600 to 604, 701 to 705, 700-A.1 to 700-A.5)",
      "The district tables set a minimum distance between buildings (single-family detached): CM 100 ft, R-1 60 ft, R-2 60 ft (70 ft with on-lot water and sewage), CR-2 50 ft, RI and RI-A 100 ft. Whether it applies between the house and a detached accessory apartment is not said. Ask the Zoning Officer",
      "At least two off-street parking spaces for each dwelling unit, none in the front yard, side and rear parking screened from the street and neighbors (H-3.4a)",
      "A Bucks County Department of Health permit certifying the sewage facilities for two family uses, and evidence the water supply serves the apartment without harming neighbors' supply (H-3.4b, d)",
      "New construction meets the yard and setback rules for a single-family dwelling in the district. The 12 ft (or 6 ft) accessory building setback of 1000.E.4 does not apply (H-3.4c)",
      "An attached apartment keeps the look of a single-family house. One in an accessory building keeps the look of a garage, barn or similar building. When the family member use ends, the space reverts to a permitted use (H-3.4e, f)",
      "Residential conversion (use B-16): an existing dwelling into more than one dwelling, or an accessory building into one dwelling, if the building existed at least 15 years before the Joint Municipal Zoning Ordinance was adopted. Conditional use in CM and CR-1 (non-cluster), R-1 and QA, special exception in VR-1. Lot area per dwelling unit at least the single-family minimum, 2 parking spaces per unit, added units at least 600 sq ft (efficiency), 700 (one bedroom) or 950 (two bedrooms) (803 B-16)",
      "Conflicting text, ask: B-16.8 names CM, but the CM use lists (401) do not list B-16. VC-1 and VC-2 list B-16 by special exception, QA-A by conditional use and TC-2 by right (600, 600.1, 700-A.5, 604), but B-16.8 does not name them",
      "VC-2 permits a twin house (B-5) and a duplex (B-6) by right. With a sewer facility the lot minimum (3,000 sq ft) applies to each dwelling unit (600.1A.1, 600.1B note 1)",
      "CR-2: the performance table gives a 30,000 sq ft single-family lot, the dimensional table 20,000 sq ft (403B, 403C). Conflicting text, ask"
    ],
    "notes": "Zoning office: Newtown Township (Bucks County) Zoning Officer. Joint Zoning Hearing Boards under Article XV. Read on eCode360 (NE3758, Newtown Area Zoning Jointure) in a browser, one page at a time, on 2026-11-14. eCode360 NE1450 'Township of Newtown' is Newtown Township in Delaware County and was not used. The first code search (all content) for 'accessory dwelling', 'accessory apartment', 'in-law', ECHO, granny, 'family dwelling', relative, caretaker, 'housekeeping unit', 'guest house', 'accessory unit', 'living quarters' and conversion showed the family definition and Residential Conversion (B-16) listings. The residential accessory apartment (H-3.4) was found by reading use H-3 and confirmed by a search for 'accessory apartment', 'accessory building' and 'accessory structure'. Article IV read in full for JM, CM, CR-1, CR-2, R-1, R-2 and VR-1. Fix round 2026-11-14: Articles V, VI, VII and VII-A read in full (print pages), the VR-4 tables (409B, C) and the R-1 table (404C) read again. The R-2 table (405C) was read in the same page."
  },
